{
  "format": "sfxgen/1",
  "name": "Firework rocket",
  "description": "A rocket at a town display, watched from the square. The fuse lights and it leaves the tube with a short fizzing 'fsst'. It climbs, screaming: a whistle (noise in a narrow pipe) that rises with a fast warble and thins as it gets higher and farther. A moment of silence. Then the shell bursts high overhead: a broad, unpitched 'BOOM' of noise that opens bright and closes dark, a heavy hollow thump under it and, for a big shell, a deep rumble of pushed air rolling on after it. Then the stars, later the bigger the shell: a long spell of thick crackling spread across the sky as they burn out, drifting down, while the bang rolls back off the buildings round the square.",
  "tags": [
    "explosion",
    "firework",
    "rocket",
    "whistle",
    "celebration",
    "burst",
    "crackle",
    "sky",
    "festival"
  ],
  "duration": "auto",
  "seed": 58,
  "output": {
    "channels": 2
  },
